<title>UK: BA strike to be resolved by two sides-Blair.</title>
<headline>BA strike to be resolved by two sides-Blair.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Prime Minister Tony Blair made clear on Wednesday that the government would keep out of the industrial dispute at British Airways Plc, saying it was a matter to be resolved by the two parties involved.</p>
<p>Asked about the dispute during Prime Minister's question time in parliament, Blair said he hoped the dispute would be resolved as quickly as possible and sympathised with travellers affected.</p>
<p>But he added: &quot;It has to be resolved by management and trade unions.&quot; -- London Newsroom +44 171 5427767</p>
</text>
